# T27887 — Verify vlan-based QinQ interoperability with vlan translation — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-30 — UNSUPPORTED

Verdict: UNSUPPORTED. The case tests VLAN-based QinQ: the global per-VLAN mapping
`vlan-stacking vlan <inner> outer-vlan <outer>`, which T27895/T27989 in the same AWPTCM folder say
"cannot be applied per interface". That command does not exist on either IE520
(awplus_main-20260923-20). `vlan-stacking ?` in global config gives `% Unrecognized command` on the
stack and on the IE520-sa, and `show vlan ?` offers no `stacking`. The licence bits ARE on: every
stack member (1, 3, 4) and the SA carry FULL with VlanDT, VLAN-TRANS-FULL and VLAN-TRANS-LITE
enabled. So the licence bit is on and the CLI is absent (flagged to the sentinel as an observation,
13:03).

Supplementary evidence (NOT graded): the nearest double-tagging features the platform does offer,
each tested together with VLAN translation on the same port.
- Port-based QinQ (`switchport vlan-stacking`) + translation on one provider port: config accepted,
  and the translation acts on the OUTER tag, as the case's precondition expects. 100/100 frames
  each way.
- The per-VLAN double-tag inside translation (`switchport vlan translation vlan <wire> outer-vlan
  <outer>`): it REPLACED the customer tag instead of pushing an outer one. Observation O-2, below.

Run labelled: clean (supplementary stages only; the graded verdict rests on the CLI refusal).

Operator: bench-runner subagent (sentinel = parent session device-testing-ba, /test-mode shape A).
Queue: IE520/CAMPAIGN-QUEUE-2026-09-29.md row 13. Case text: ck.db zephyr AWPTCM-T27887 — no steps;
precondition "vlan-based QinQ and vlan translation should not be used on the same port If both
vlan-based QinQ and vlan translation are applied on the same port, the outer vlan tag will be used
for translation". Terrence's decision (2026-09-30): check the VLAN double-tagging licence bit and
whether the commands are enabled "in any way".

